<title>USA: Faulding unit gets FDA nod for product.</title>
<headline>Faulding unit gets FDA nod for product.</headline>
<dateline>ELIZABETH, N.J. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Faulding Inc said on Friday its Purepac Pharmaceutical Co unit won final approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market etodolac anti-inflammatory tablets, a generic version of Lodine.</p>
<p>The tablets are to be used to treat osteoarthritis and pain. Lodine is made by Wyeth-Ayerst Laboratories Inc, a unit of American Home Products Corp.</p>
<p>Faulding said it will begin shipping its etodolac product on March 1.</p>
</text>
